@startuml Abstract Factory Pattern

' Define the styles
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam classBackgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam classBorderColor #dee2e6
skinparam arrowColor #6c757d
skinparam stereotypeCBackgroundColor #e9ecef

' Title
title Abstract Factory Pattern - Basic Structure

' Abstract Products
interface ProductA <<AbstractProduct>> {
  +operationA(): void
}

interface ProductB <<AbstractProduct>> {
  +operationB(): void
}

' Abstract Factory
interface AbstractFactory <<AbstractFactory>> {
  +createProductA(): ProductA
  +createProductB(): ProductB
}

' Concrete Products - Family 1
class ProductA1 <<ConcreteProduct>> {
  +operationA(): void
}

class ProductB1 <<ConcreteProduct>> {
  +operationB(): void
}

' Concrete Products - Family 2
class ProductA2 <<ConcreteProduct>> {
  +operationA(): void
}

class ProductB2 <<ConcreteProduct>> {
  +operationB(): void
}

' Concrete Factories
class ConcreteFactory1 <<ConcreteFactory>> {
  +createProductA(): ProductA
  +createProductB(): ProductB
}

class ConcreteFactory2 <<ConcreteFactory>> {
  +createProductA(): ProductA
  +createProductB(): ProductB
}

' Relationships - Interface implementations
ProductA <|.. ProductA1
ProductA <|.. ProductA2
ProductB <|.. ProductB1
ProductB <|.. ProductB2

' Factory relationships
AbstractFactory <|.. ConcreteFactory1
AbstractFactory <|.. ConcreteFactory2

' Factory creates products
ConcreteFactory1 ..> ProductA1 : creates >
ConcreteFactory1 ..> ProductB1 : creates >
ConcreteFactory2 ..> ProductA2 : creates >
ConcreteFactory2 ..> ProductB2 : creates >

' Pattern component notes
note right of AbstractFactory
  <b>Abstract Factory</b>
  Declares interface for creating
  families of related product objects.

  <b>Role:</b>
  • Defines creation methods for
    each abstract product type
  • Ensures all factories provide
    complete product families
end note

note left of ProductA
  <b>Abstract Product A</b>
  Declares interface for one type
  of product object.

  <b>Role:</b>
  • Defines contract for products
  • Multiple variants implement
    this interface
end note

note bottom of ConcreteFactory1
  <b>Concrete Factory 1</b>
  Creates <b>Family 1</b> of products.

  <b>Role:</b>
  • Implements AbstractFactory interface
  • Creates ProductA1 and ProductB1
  • Ensures products work together
end note

note bottom of ConcreteFactory2
  <b>Concrete Factory 2</b>
  Creates <b>Family 2</b> of products.

  <b>Role:</b>
  • Implements AbstractFactory interface
  • Creates ProductA2 and ProductB2
  • Ensures products work together
end note

note bottom of ProductA1
  <b>Concrete Product A1</b>
  Belongs to <b>Family 1</b>.

  <b>Role:</b>
  • Implements ProductA interface
  • Designed to work with ProductB1
  • Created by ConcreteFactory1
end note

note bottom of ProductB2
  <b>Concrete Product B2</b>
  Belongs to <b>Family 2</b>.

  <b>Role:</b>
  • Implements ProductB interface
  • Designed to work with ProductA2
  • Created by ConcreteFactory2
end note

' Pattern overview note
note as PatternOverview
  <b>Abstract Factory Pattern</b>

  <b>Intent:</b>
  Provide an interface for creating families
  of related or dependent objects without
  specifying their concrete classes.

  <b>Key Concept:</b>
  Products from the same factory are designed
  to work together as a family.
  • Family 1: ProductA1 + ProductB1
  • Family 2: ProductA2 + ProductB2

  <b>Client Usage:</b>
  AbstractFactory factory = new ConcreteFactory1();
  ProductA productA = factory.createProductA();
  ProductB productB = factory.createProductB();
  // productA and productB work together consistently
end note

@enduml